  "notes": "Near-black pro video tool (Electron 43) with 7px-rounded panels outlined in #273035 on slightly lighter #101416 sidebars. Blue (#1f8bff-ish) used for current step circles, selected option card outline and primary Export button; cyan for credit links; neon green for success/quality ratings; coral red for Cancel. Many controls are disabled while analysis runs. Central grid shows the source clip plus derived control passes (camera path overlay with a perspective grid and camera icon, pose skeleton, depth, edges, masks, 3D stick figure canvas). Export presets are letter-monogram tiles in brand-ish colors (S teal, C purple, B orange, R green, K blue). Steppers with -/+ buttons for numeric settings (Temporal Window, Max People). Capture was taken with a 2283px window so view tiles appear stretched."
